<title>GERMANY: German November unemployment rises 50,000.</title>
<headline>German November unemployment rises 50,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German unemployment rose 50,000 to a seasonally adjusted 4.1 million in November, the Federal Labour Office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The unemployment rate, which is based on unadjusted data, rose to 10.3 percent, compared with 10.1 percent in October.</p>
<p>The rise was in line with forecasts by independent analysts.</p>
<p>In western Germany, the number of people out of work on a seasonally adjusted basis rose 34,000 to 2.942 million.</p>
<p>Eastern Germany added 17,000 to unemployment rolls, with the total number of jobless rising to 1.176 million.</p>
<p>On an unadjusted basis, the number of Germans out of work rose 3.942 million in November 3.866 million.</p>
</text>
